[{"id":"VRCE-7-30-1","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":30,"verse":1,"english":"The highly powerful Mahendra being thus defeated by Ravana's son, all the celestials, taking the patriarch Brahmä before them, went to Lanka.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.71,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-30-1"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7030001","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"c1e163d98b88617cf097b3f31871ea840ab4f140f4a5947270b876378a6bf35f","compact":"db5f070afba35ff6f8c2465289067e15f1b2d6225330e8b5ae201e9fc3845669","nasal":"2118f5c04a48328561865e023da4fd385e1d96c3d717c7c9351ea9f06d4a0b16"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-30-2","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":30,"verse":2,"english":"Having obtained Rāvana encircled by his sons and brothers the Patriarch, stationed in the welkin, calmly said.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.623,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-30-2"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7030002","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"a6d2058568a92c85a1e00b6cf8ca756ee74d5cda32230052d942cf79f6328d32","compact":"4070e54ec0248ca27bfdd4aa021afac97d874f1df5309fe543b1c18f763e6072","nasal":"937dd09bc011cdee9c1b88c91f5d6bfd273a3ec5f2572c88dc0380152b3fa368"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-30-3","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":30,"verse":3,"english":"My son, Ravana, I have been pleased with your son in the conflict. Oh! what wonderful prowess, what strength-equal or greater than your.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.613,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-30-3"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7030003","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"d033d7c8cfb777832f21dc26839a54f5300f36617c97fb3fb9ef629d9b71b8fb","compact":"de74373dc35be79f23b748d997ef0dd665199ae6b040e8ec3adc1d36e5bfbfc3","nasal":"de74373dc35be79f23b748d997ef0dd665199ae6b040e8ec3adc1d36e5bfbfc3"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-30-4","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":30,"verse":4,"english":"You have, by your own prowess, conquered the three worlds — your promise has borne fruits-I have been pleased with you-both the father and son.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.738,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-30-4"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7030004","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"4b0392496c44f6e96778365d97bd845704c8ef1f2f03dd010e3a58c34a608513","compact":"d84badbfa2717ea9259741d944b7308bc1913da763d0ed4abf3e33404d7b4bfd","nasal":"d84badbfa2717ea9259741d944b7308bc1913da763d0ed4abf3e33404d7b4bfd"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-30-5","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":30,"verse":5,"english":"O Rāvana, this your son is highly powerful and gifted with great strength and he shall be celebrated in the world under the appellation of 'Indrajit' or the conqueror of Indra.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.267,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-30-5"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7030005","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"c41ca7367be71cae4cd208eb872969fa7f427bfcb3f76f817c57b0063caf2dd5","compact":"ff4f698d025a9166de664344c4bf0e405a7bd56ecd59fed0852585df410f6e9e","nasal":"a7851f7a5496d1b8a22906af8f719b6a817dbf97e0764c79c7ddd04d3e8fa430"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-30-6","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":30,"verse":6,"english":"The Raksasa shall be powerful and irrepressible, by those help, O King, the celestials have been brought under your subjection.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.314,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-30-6"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7030006","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"4dc1cf4ddfd120bb3a200a3e0a9c5abe58bd94926ba816caefcb5003469485f5","compact":"d823cac7b74584a265c822629101b199ec653f64b765734cf40b9307ee53d151","nasal":"d823cac7b74584a265c822629101b199ec653f64b765734cf40b9307ee53d151"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-30-7","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":30,"verse":7,"english":"Do you therefore, O you having long arms, release Mahendra, she chastiser of Pāka and for setting him free what do you want from the celestials?","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.879,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-30-7"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7030007","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"a38a2e76f932c8621bceb83acbb260e5988a56d48b10b401499e472d7ed359dd","compact":"5e0926f6bea01c67c6977b54c94e3f8011d1e8462f8dfb348a2e6b3103bfc99c","nasal":"8f4bf3d4d2b5b29627094d1655f6080d6e444394d705eb6b8d4b9d7fab873974"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-30-8","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":30,"verse":8,"english":"Thereupon the highly powerful Indrajit-the subduer of enemies, said: \"If do you say so, O god, I pray for immortality.\"","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.746,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-30-8"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7030008","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"df3d246074b89b96935b0d5d71708b7747fe7beb6ea73ed3bbe2b2499b381182","compact":"b53d70fc27f46198881de787296320346ec7eca7a7a957bd30a94d6e7fbe5722","nasal":"862565b1c079cf88b1b64e967490fb47e9f49160fc7629b702aa6bc9d625c189"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-30-9","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":30,"verse":9,"english":"Thereat the highly powerful patriarch said to Meghanāda, “There is none perfectly immortal on earth among created beings, birds, quadrupeds and other highly powerful beings.”","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.273,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-30-9"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7030009","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"342f0f204b9213f5cdf4d9ea85edf04cd4194aac444db5e10970c12ee78533d3","compact":"045743efe1d39d71eaccc55d5e404b5764baf1837705d07e7ca09ccc381bbcfb","nasal":"045743efe1d39d71eaccc55d5e404b5764baf1837705d07e7ca09ccc381bbcfb"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-30-10","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":30,"verse":10,"english":"Hear, then, what I want in exchange for releasing Sakra. May a chariot with horses rise up from fire when I shall offer sacrifices to it, being desirous of vanquishing my enemies in the conflict. And may I be immortal as long as I shall remain on that car. This is the boon I have resolved upon praying for.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.329,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-30-11"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7030010","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"4d37f56344a48a972cc7fa32291d4400a7cc89ca8c536b3924d8dafb0953b662","compact":"3f62b799ab0f50a6ff028b81ea95515e52c7a3bfd1c4a6eb78a78919e5cdf60c","nasal":"c7aba83c7b300c64e2caf28d69c268f4a74dfda2589d395c981b47a6670991df"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-30-11","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":30,"verse":11,"english":"Hear, then, what I want in exchange for releasing Sakra. May a chariot with horses rise up from fire when I shall offer sacrifices to it, being desirous of vanquishing my enemies in the conflict. And may I be immortal as long as I shall remain on that car. This is the boon I have resolved upon praying for.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.388,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-30-11"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7030011","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"af8dc79203fccea3401763a8c519f96aeeef4162f2ba50ed53b728651308b4a9","compact":"c93ed9596c3ec5278ff6522b8c00131f888c989e9bf2e2489f0cc735331c3c98","nasal":"3e66091e08be63a0c352194f1fde0fbacf053c8db31a4270e9e8f8e28b3e40c8"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-30-12","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":30,"verse":12,"english":"May I meet with destruction, O deity, whenever I shall engage in fight without finishing my offerings to fire.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.567,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-30-12"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7030012","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"c9c7b1b141512cee2adae50f3abf253cc06bb9521e40c1cb32da907afef176c0","compact":"b6e373f8e9ccfc68e9d945aad73df2588cde182f08a92e367c544ad7f36143d4","nasal":"b6e373f8e9ccfc68e9d945aad73df2588cde182f08a92e367c544ad7f36143d4"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-30-13","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":30,"verse":13,"english":"All others, O god, attain to immortality by virtue of devout penances but I shall acquire that by dint of my own prowess.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.847,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-30-13"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7030013","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"3c1569e6f10f8eda90182bafa9f3e2b9bcace689982e4e3448de70bf45836a16","compact":"d63e6a443fcbc34650045bf9bcfc080791da98b00fc8dfa0041dc731fd61bb37","nasal":"d63e6a443fcbc34650045bf9bcfc080791da98b00fc8dfa0041dc731fd61bb37"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-30-14","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":30,"verse":14,"english":"Where to the grand-father replied saying \"so be it.\" Thereupon Meghanäda released Indra and the celestials returned to their own abode.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.667,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-30-14"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7030014","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"528dd2cc1f929a34f8d36e1429c79f01e602963ad983f05bb027cf36a7df40e4","compact":"3af57bda3c6ba40369c9c30d024fa063eb0e9e01169a8455a33625e57371c878","nasal":"bdfcd45cc1e1f8c064d6362b447ac7b5feb23e747f2e5e673cd546ad49de1d6e"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-30-15","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":30,"verse":15,"english":"In the interval, O Rāma, Indra became poorly, divested of his immortal brilliance, stricken with anxiety and pensive.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.545,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-30-15"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7030015","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"ee06351a0074cc87918c7b7d1e818be9980f9281ff09ef3ba9a34e985d9e609d","compact":"84f6de4941d8478837646b1be1e5f1658d1bb0711c11d483eeb5fe64ca770f55","nasal":"bfd6e1aafbb16948e22ea35b192c51c3db6cb45bc32c0513a9890a91c1f1bf5d"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-30-16","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":30,"verse":16,"english":"Beholding him in that plight the grand-father of the deities said:-O performer of hundred sacrifices, why did you formerly perpetrate that mighty iniquity?","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.433,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-30-16"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7030016","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"cf0c29619a0ab74065da1ac72ca768af52c69f2d74df301be37fa15af378a3f4","compact":"e11f48e82062e02fcbe21f9a7c02cc4b785c62b33fe289d72a182c9871198eaa","nasal":"ecaf62dc24c8ab73f7fd9375044c2b91e968a58bb9addf6df593c5cc74e0dcb2"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-30-17","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":30,"verse":17,"english":"O Chief of the immortals! O lord!, some creatures were all of the same colour, same speech, and same appearance.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.625,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-30-17"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7030017","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"948719ce8b13901b830d3f92a5356c13ba767f2afe6202decc80a0e70e6dd00c","compact":"f8ff592d52996d7d62eaca7ab948109373989b0da35733bc3af5b15408f16b17","nasal":"ec0934d280100ba701db345889033b111b72b04f08f1dbc49c3ce159c64c0582"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-30-18","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":30,"verse":18,"english":"There was no difference visible in their appearance or marks. Thereupon, with wholeminded-ness, I began to think of these created beings.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.831,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-30-18"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7030018","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"c7dc8618bccc63a7644d26e87e25b3e9a3c483998aa1d5ffb565f3f065a4e4dc","compact":"c11e6e86d04c8e2f76813a56f44207897767ea19fbc140beca04e1d55e1bdd40","nasal":"ed75780186babd372b817525fa77187362e6493a91dc3f7fa6547d97d4255bae"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-30-19","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":30,"verse":19,"english":"And I created a female distinct from them. Collecting all those limbs that were most excellent among the created, I made a female under the name of Ahalyä. Hal means uglinessone born from Hal is called Halya. That female was known as Ahalyā because she had nothing blameable in her, I gave her that name.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-30-19"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7030019","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"ba7110669c01c1c677bf5bfa2454e2a79efad5579d5989e200bac869998d02d2","compact":"9ebd4eea7a90e6a1be83ffd2794ffcbbccb705359ba3955334e5f0e98ce90bac","nasal":"bc080aec9cb21fc53ad49b4b4b92bbc00aabbc0d41b7b83fec064dc70418cbc4"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-30-20","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":30,"verse":20,"english":"And I created a female distinct from them. Collecting all those limbs that were most excellent among the created, I made a female under the name of Ahalyä. Hal means uglinessone born from Hal is called Halya. That female was known as Ahalyā because she had nothing blameable in her, I gave her that name.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.79,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-30-19"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7030020","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"f3161fa52b4e5ac88fdf955fbff6bdcf55d1127951df9e97e2df694001ef1f22","compact":"4c917c2edc4dacd379847bf0d2c7c3d2a56a533f79025877bf6396c60e6ca5f4","nasal":"4c917c2edc4dacd379847bf0d2c7c3d2a56a533f79025877bf6396c60e6ca5f4"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-30-21","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":30,"verse":21,"english":"Having created that female I was thinking, O king of the celestials! O foremost of the deities!, on whom I should confer her.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.687,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-30-20"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7030021","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"282ff7d96ff9ff9fff61b3e2f32360eea84fc0b780d4c95e9a14d4f47cc6b293","compact":"9c764af8a20d879b8a9786947d60d0943b78811fe7c6a6c3674223a416c85038","nasal":"704ce4f12e08dcefc6390749a3e685d29364a5bc690650345fdc00c08abad545"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-30-22","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":30,"verse":22,"english":"Being proud of dignity, O Sakra, O lord, O Purandara you did regard her in your mind as your spouse.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.857,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-30-21"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7030022","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"4240ff51d691be0f5704a00eaa0eb0b42770cf5ee8